// The inline content of a Markdown file, as guests (decision 0055's `embed`, decision 0238). tree-sitter-md reads a
// Markdown file in two grammars: the block grammar gives the file's tree (headings, lists, paragraphs, code blocks),
// and each `inline` and `pipe_table_cell` node of it holds text in the inline grammar (`markdown-inline`: emphasis,
// links, code spans, inline HTML). Each such node is a guest of that grammar, a part of its host ("fragment").
//
//   > Some *text* and a [link](u)       block: block_quote > paragraph > inline
//   > on two lines.                     inline guest: emphasis, inline_link > link_text, link_destination
//
// A guest's text is the node's without the block continuations inside it (the `> ` above), and its nodes have the
// file's lines and columns.
embed(d, n, "markdown-inline", "fragment") :- node(d, n, "inline", _, _).
embed(d, n, "markdown-inline", "fragment") :- node(d, n, "pipe_table_cell", _, _).
